# ============================================================================
# Epistemic Resonance Protocol — N4L arrow definitions
#
# These relations are used by the coordinator zome's N4L export
# (dna/coordinator/src/lib.rs, ToN4L trait).
#
# LOADING: this file is NOT read automatically by placing it "alongside"
# SSTorytime's standard SSTconfig/ files, despite what an earlier version
# of this comment (and the README) claimed. The real N4L binary's
# ReadConfig() only ever loads a hardcoded list of 6 exact filenames
# (arrows-LT-1.sst, arrows-NR-0.sst, arrows-CN-2.sst, arrows-EP-3.sst,
# annotations.sst, closures.sst) — confirmed by reading cmd/N4L/N4L.go.
# A 7th file, however named, is silently never read. To actually use
# these relations, merge each of this file's three sections into the
# matching one of those 6 files (this one's `- leadsto` body into
# arrows-LT-1.sst, `- contains` into arrows-CN-2.sst, `- properties`
# into arrows-EP-3.sst), each as its own `:: epistemic ::` context block
# — this file's own three-section layout mirrors that split for exactly
# this reason.
#
# VERIFICATION STATUS: run end-to-end against the real N4L Go binary
# (built from github.com/markburgess/SSTorytime, cmd/N4L) with a live
# PostgreSQL backend (N4L's Open() pings the DB unconditionally, even
# for -v/no-upload runs) and a real Rust-generated export sample. This
# file's vocabulary itself parses cleanly once merged as described
# above. Two further defects were found and fixed as a result of that
# run, both now reflected in dna/coordinator/src/lib.rs: (1) every
# ToN4L impl's output is missing the `- <chapter>` declaration N4L
# requires before any other line (fatal: "Declarations outside a
# section or chapter at line 1") — export_to_n4l now emits one; (2)
# WorldlineTrace/Constitution baked a loop index directly into relation
# names ("covers period 0", "promise 0 action", ...), which can never
# match a fixed, pre-declared arrow vocabulary — fixed by moving the
# index to N4L's comma-delimited context-tag syntax ("covers period,p0")
# on a static, registered name instead. `has dht hash`,
# `replication attempted`, `promise domain`, and `condition param` were
# also missing from this file outright and are now registered above.
# See README §5.2/§5.3 for the full account.
#
# A further pass (verified via a real N4L -u upload into a live SSTorytime
# instance, see sstorytime/setup.sh + sstorytime/ingest.sh) found this file
# had also redefined three arrows SSTorytime's own stock SSTconfig/ vocabulary
# already provides under the same long name — "has description", "describes",
# and "has condition" — which N4L flags as a long-name redefinition warning
# (non-fatal, but a real vocabulary collision, not just noise). `has
# description` is genuinely used (Membrane::to_n4l) and now simply resolves
# via the stock arrow of that name instead of a redundant local one; no Rust
# code change was needed, since to_n4l only emits the relation text, not a
# short code. `describes` and `has condition` were never emitted by any
# ToN4L impl at all and were removed outright as dead entries.
#
# Per SSTorytime's four-type model (see docs/N4L.md):
#   0 similarity  — undirected closeness
#   1 leadsto     — causal/temporal order, one thing follows/affects another
#   2 contains    — membership, part-of
#   3 properties  — descriptive attributes
# ============================================================================

- leadsto

    # A critique doesn't just describe a claim, it acts on its standing —
    # so it's causal/affecting, not merely descriptive.
    + critiques (crit)       - is critiqued by (critby)
    + contradicts (contra)   - is contradicted by (contraby)
    + flags (flag)           - is flagged by (flagby)
    + adopts species (adopts) - is adopted by (adoptby)
    + retracts (retr)        - is retracted by (retrby)
    + replaced by (replby)   - replaces (repl)
    + promoted to (promto)   - promoted from (promfrom)
    + replies to (replyto)   - has reply (hasreply)
    + imported from (impfrom) - was imported to (impto)

- contains

    + has evidence (ev)      - is evidence for (evfor)
    + requires promise (reqp) - is required promise of (reqpof)
    + covers period (covp)   - is period of (covpof)
    + has promise (haspr)    - is promise of (prof)

- properties

    + asserted by (assertby)   - is the assertion of (assertof)
    + has domain (dom)         - is domain of (domof)
    + has confidence (conf)    - is confidence of (confof)
    + critique mode (cmode)    - is mode of critique (cmodeof)
    + has tag (tag)            - is tag of (tagof)
    + has source url (srcurl)  - is url source for (srcurlof)
    + evidence type (evtype)   - is type of evidence (evtypeof)
    + bridged via (bridge)     - is bridge for (bridgeof)
    + bridge id (bridgeid)     - is bridge id of (bridgeidof)
    + created by (createdby)   - is creator of (creatorof)
    + expires at (expat)       - is expiry of (expof)
    + has checksum (chk)       - is checksum of (chkof)
    + has expertise tag (exp)  - is expertise tag of (expof2)
    + sample action (sampact)  - is sample for (sampof)
    + has entry count (ecount) - is count of (ecountof)
    + promise action (promact) - is action of promise (promactof)
    + promise modality (mod)   - is modality of (modof)
    + condition type (condtype) - is type of condition (condtypeof)
    + founded on constitution (foundedon) - is constitution founding (foundingof)
    + target type (targtype)   - is target type of (targtypeof)
    + has dht hash (dhth)       - is dht hash of (dhthof)
    + replication attempted (repat) - is attempt of replication (repatof)
    + promise domain (promdom) - is domain of promise (promdomof)
    + condition param (condparam) - is parameter of condition (condparamof)
    + pattern kind (patkind)   - is kind of pattern (patkindof)
